[SPEAKER_01]: How would the person go about in that environment?

7
00:01:01,459 --> 00:01:10,864
[SPEAKER_01]: What would be the necessary things, necessary practical things for them to do, consider, uphold, and so on, so that they can actually develop those precepts?

8
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:24,130
[SPEAKER_02]: The thing is, one thing that's very commonly mentioned in the suttas is that the quality of your friendships has a very direct impact on the qualities that you have in your mind.

9
00:01:24,210 --> 00:01:25,130
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the people that you're

10
00:01:26,826 --> 00:01:36,470
[SPEAKER_02]: If those people have sensual values, even if you try to cultivate the opposite values, by default, the current is taking you in the opposite direction.

11
00:01:37,451 --> 00:01:49,636
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you want to be careful that you're not... that you're minimizing contact with people who value sensuality, who would find fault with you for trying to practice the dhamma.

12
00:01:49,997 --> 00:01:52,858
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't completely sometimes remove those people from your life, but

13
00:01:53,801 --> 00:02:01,886
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're actively maintaining friendships with them, not just like, oh, I have to talk to him because he's my co-worker or something.

14
00:02:01,906 --> 00:02:09,951
[SPEAKER_02]: You're actively maintaining relationships with them and you are, by that token, you're giving their opinions weight.

15
00:02:10,912 --> 00:02:16,035
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's going to influence your mind, going to kind of taint your views with these wrong emphases.

16
00:02:16,095 --> 00:02:17,115
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's the first thing.

17
00:02:18,056 --> 00:02:20,778
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, secondly, you want to recognize, well, even if

18
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:23,751
[SPEAKER_02]: Other people are doing whatever they might be doing.

19
00:02:24,451 --> 00:02:27,132
[SPEAKER_02]: That doesn't absolve you from your responsibility.

20
00:02:27,893 --> 00:02:33,695
[SPEAKER_02]: So, as there's that sutta where the Buddha said, eh... others will be killing, here we will not be killing.

21
00:02:33,835 --> 00:02:36,537
[SPEAKER_02]: Others will be stealing, here we will not be stealing.

22
00:02:37,097 --> 00:02:42,899
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you... you certainly shouldn't expect your environment to be perfectly conducive.

23
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:48,502
[SPEAKER_02]: That, like, oh, because everybody around me is... is eh... going the same direction, that's why I can do it.

24
00:02:49,611 --> 00:02:51,032
[SPEAKER_02]: More often than not, that will not be the case.

25
00:02:51,092 --> 00:02:57,397
[SPEAKER_02]: Even in the monastery, for that matter, you will not find everyone being 100% on the same page.

26
00:02:58,058 --> 00:03:04,343
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you have to feel that weight of... Yeah, like, I could do the opposite.

27
00:03:05,103 --> 00:03:06,965
[SPEAKER_02]: I could choose to give in to sensuality.

28
00:03:07,025 --> 00:03:09,407
[SPEAKER_02]: I could choose to be careless.

29
00:03:10,007 --> 00:03:11,729
[SPEAKER_02]: But then, I will be paying the price for that.

30
00:03:11,889 --> 00:03:18,194
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not like the weight of tradition or the weight of a group that's making you do it.

31
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:27,309
[SPEAKER_02]: If it is, then your determination will crack as soon as those external factors are compromised.

32
00:03:27,369 --> 00:03:35,138
[SPEAKER_02]: Any other practical... Yeah, well, another thing to keep in mind is...

33
00:03:37,357 --> 00:03:41,900
[SPEAKER_02]: You might have to, depending on how proliferated you've been, you might have to take it gradually.

34
00:03:42,581 --> 00:04:05,818
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you know, when we talk about, eh... celibacy is necessary, you have to completely give up sensuality, that's... that should be your value, that should be your goal, but you want to recognize that if you try to take that all of a sudden, too much all at once, you might end up, eh... you know, slingshotting back into your old habits, because it was just too much for you to bear.

35
00:04:06,418 --> 00:04:06,679
[SPEAKER_02]: So,

36
00:04:07,627 --> 00:04:08,888
[SPEAKER_02]: You want to keep that as your goal.

37
00:04:08,948 --> 00:04:15,693
[SPEAKER_02]: You want to feel the inadequacy of the remaining sensual habits that you might have.

38
00:04:16,353 --> 00:04:22,978
[SPEAKER_02]: You want to avoid shifting the goalposts and trying to justify them, because I'm a lay person, it's fine, or something.

39
00:04:24,519 --> 00:04:28,101
[SPEAKER_02]: But then, at the same time, you want to work towards it gradually.

40
00:04:28,141 --> 00:04:33,505
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if you haven't been keeping the five precepts, then start with that.

41
00:04:34,546 --> 00:04:34,846
[SPEAKER_02]: If you

42
00:04:35,850 --> 00:04:39,992
[SPEAKER_02]: If you have been keeping the five precepts already, then start building it up.

43
00:04:42,693 --> 00:04:50,457
[SPEAKER_02]: Start removing sensual indulgences that you know are completely unnecessary, and you just give in to them out of weakness.

44
00:04:50,557 --> 00:04:59,000
[SPEAKER_02]: Take on the eight precepts on occasion, like on the uposita, and then work towards making that your permanent mode of being.

45
00:04:59,481 --> 00:05:02,122
[SPEAKER_02]: Because it's about seeing

46
00:05:03,652 --> 00:05:15,340
[SPEAKER_02]: Again, it's... it's... you shouldn't see it just like, oh, because this is a requirement on that theoretical level, you should start feeling yourself the peril of being still involved in the sensual domain.

47
00:05:15,621 --> 00:05:16,721
[SPEAKER_01]: How does one do that?

48
00:05:16,801 --> 00:05:21,405
[SPEAKER_01]: Say, for example, they... a person is not associating with bad friends,

49
00:05:22,691 --> 00:05:39,178
[SPEAKER_01]: ...is paying attention to their environment, in the sense of, like, as much as of an input as they have, they're exercising that, so they're not carelessly going into the sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches, unless they have to, minimizing exposure to that.

50
00:05:40,359 --> 00:05:48,942
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, when the pressures get too much, people still might be breaking the presets, even without the external prompts, and so on.

51
00:05:49,643 --> 00:05:49,923
[SPEAKER_01]: So,

52
00:05:51,330 --> 00:06:03,194
[SPEAKER_01]: How would one train in that, to not fail there, and to obviously increase the restraint without, as you said, kind of slingshotting back?

53
00:06:05,814 --> 00:06:17,458
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how would you... those values that you talk about, the danger, that it's dangerous for me, engaging with it, not just kind of the secondary dangers and warnings, how can they directly begin to see that?

54
00:06:20,027 --> 00:06:33,097
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, the first thing is, you might be tempted to not want to feel regret, not want to feel shame, when you do something unwholesome, and you give in to sensuality.

55
00:06:33,117 --> 00:06:38,402
[SPEAKER_02]: You might... like, that's exactly when people resort to the views of, oh, well, you're a lay person, it's not a big deal.

56
00:06:39,002 --> 00:06:39,422
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not...

57
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:40,143
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm absolved.

58
00:06:40,183 --> 00:06:41,784
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm absolved from responsibility for this.

59
00:06:41,924 --> 00:06:42,705
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not a coincidence.

60
00:06:42,745 --> 00:06:49,150
[SPEAKER_02]: It's because you don't want to feel the the weight that comes when you see, oh, I had this goal and I actually walked against it.

61
00:06:50,700 --> 00:07:03,222
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the first thing is, like, you will not be able to properly develop that value if you don't want to feel ashamed, because that shame is the symptom of the value being maintained.

62
00:07:04,383 --> 00:07:08,503
[SPEAKER_02]: The shame is what tells you, like, oh, I'm actually maintaining sight of what I should have done.

63
00:07:09,784 --> 00:07:10,764
[SPEAKER_02]: So... To not deny it.

64
00:07:10,984 --> 00:07:11,324
[SPEAKER_02]: Exactly.

65
00:07:11,784 --> 00:07:16,645
[SPEAKER_02]: So, don't try to push it away, because, as the Buddha himself said,

66
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:26,025
[SPEAKER_02]: Fear of wrongdoing is one of the basic faculties on the path, on the same level as mindfulness, samādhi.

67
00:07:26,926 --> 00:07:39,613
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if you try to deny that, that's exactly how you won't be... you won't have that... you won't be developing that internal criteria that, for example, a sotāpanna is what would be driving them to make further progress.

68
00:07:39,733 --> 00:07:42,495
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, even if they might, as sometimes happen in the suttas,

69
00:07:43,570 --> 00:07:44,191
[SPEAKER_02]: Get careless.

70
00:07:44,791 --> 00:08:04,951
[SPEAKER_02]: The fact is they wouldn't be able to cover up that shame, that they know this is against the path, this is causing me harm, taking me... because the harm, the the danger of that whole thing that Siddha described has to be seen internally.

71
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:07,173
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, they wouldn't be able to cover up the shame.

72
00:08:08,213 --> 00:08:25,561
[SPEAKER_01]: And, consequently, they would not be able to develop further wrong views that are used to make them cope, to make them justify, to kind of, well, absolve them from the weight of those actions.

73
00:08:26,461 --> 00:08:34,225
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, because covering up the shame, you're covering up the first kind of gateway to recognizing the danger.

74
00:08:35,375 --> 00:08:37,135
[SPEAKER_01]: Or by not allowing it to come up, I guess.

75
00:08:37,295 --> 00:08:37,836
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

76
00:08:37,896 --> 00:08:44,417
[SPEAKER_01]: By saying, oh, this doesn't apply to me, this requirement doesn't apply to me, because otherwise you just, yeah, you would feel too unpleasant.

77
00:08:44,557 --> 00:08:47,498
[SPEAKER_02]: Right, because, yeah, it's not even that you have to fabricate the shame.

78
00:08:47,958 --> 00:08:55,840
[SPEAKER_02]: You would see that it would be there on its own, just by maintaining the perspective, this is the goal, shame is there automatically, if you contradict it.

79
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:58,601
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's not even that you have to work yourself up.

80
00:08:58,621 --> 00:09:04,582
[SPEAKER_02]: You abstain from wearing away the value of withdrawal from sensuality, you will feel shame whenever you...

81
00:09:04,850 --> 00:09:22,518
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, so if somebody is not denying the shame, so they're given the precepts, or training in them, not associating with bad friends, exercising their input as much as they can in the suitable environment, not denying shame when it arises, is there something more?

82
00:09:22,598 --> 00:09:24,119
[SPEAKER_01]: Is there any other things they can do?

83
00:09:29,142 --> 00:09:31,803
[SPEAKER_01]: In terms of their danger, sensuality, values,

84
